<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.capture.reads ~ live, or paused with its reason and since

The hook-lever stands on its own: a marker file a capture hook checks and steps aside on when present (whatever runs the `lares sense capture` and `lares sense telemetry` legs on a session event). A migration or a `lares sense teardown` then runs WITHOUT daemon-spawn contention: the minting stops at the source, with no whack-a-mole against spawned children. `lares mempalace quiesce` pauses AND drains the warm daemons in one gesture; this lever suppresses minting alone, touching no live daemon.

`hooks status` answers {hooksPaused, marker, since?, reason?}: LIVE (minting on dispatch) or PAUSED with the recorded reason and the time it began. It writes nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ is-minting-paused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`is-minting-paused` params=`~ read the lever`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a read of the marker file; it writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

